* Greatest Common Divisor — Euclid's algorithm
* gcd(252, 105) = 21, stored at GCD
*
* At each step: r = u mod v; u ← v; v ← r
* Loop until v = 0; then gcd = u

U       EQU     1000
V       EQU     1001
GCD     EQU     1002
        ORIG    U
        CON     252         * u
        CON     105         * v
        CON     0           * result

        ORIG    3000
LOOP    LDA     V           * rA = v
        CMPA    =0=         * v = 0?
        JE      DONE        * yes → gcd = u
        ENTA    0           * rA = 0  (clear high half for DIV)
        LDX     U           * rX = u
        DIV     V           * rA = u/v,  rX = u mod v
        STX     T           * T = u mod v
        LDA     V           * rA = v  (= new u)
        STA     U           * u ← v
        LDA     T           * rA = u mod v  (= new v)
        STA     V           * v ← u mod v
        JMP     LOOP
DONE    LDA     U           * gcd is in U
        STA     GCD
        HLT
T       CON     0
        END     LOOP
